kubeos-kubernetes (1.37.2-1kubeos2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * postinst: report a hold it cannot clear instead of pretending to clear it.
    apt-mark needs the dpkg lock that apt itself holds while a postinst runs, so
    releasing the old ISO's `apt-mark hold` from here always failed silently; the
    node kept a hold that would block KubeOS's own published updates. It now prints
    the command to run.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:35:00 +0530

kubeos-kubernetes (1.37.2-1kubeos1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Initial packaging: names the Kubernetes release a KubeOS node runs.
  * Ships nothing itself - it pins, with `Depends: =`, the four upstream packages
    (kubelet, kubeadm, kubectl, kubernetes-cni) that the KubeOS archive mirrors
    byte for byte from pkgs.k8s.io, so `apt upgrade` can never move Kubernetes past
    what KubeOS has vetted.
  * postinst drops the upstream pkgs.k8s.io sources line a pre-package node still
    has, and releases the `apt-mark hold` the old ISO applied.

 -- KubeOS <mail@kubeos.in>  Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:25:00 +0530
